Less than a week left. Submit your anonymized memo and financial model by Sun=
day, October 25 at 11:59 PM ET.

Your Round 1 pitch
is due this Sunday.

October 25, 2026
11:59 PM ET

Less than a week left. Please submit both your memo and financial model by th=
e deadline.

Hi teams,

Round 1 submissions for the Ivy Investment Competition are due Sunday, Octobe=
r 25 at 11:59 PM ET. Please review the requirements below and submit your tea=
m=E2=80=99s materials using the form.

Submit your Round 1 pitch
Submission link: https://forms.gle/MaTFyZdWKhz43uLs7

What to submit

An anonymized investment memo (PDF) and financial model. Enter your registere=
d Team ID and stock in the submission form. Sign in to Google to upload your =
files.

Memo body: 1,500 words maximum, excluding exhibits, footnotes, and appendix.

Entire memo: 15 pages maximum, including the one-page cover, exhibits, footno=
tes, and appendix.

Formatting: PDF; minimum 11-point font; standard margins.

Memo filename: TEAMID_TICKER_LONG.pdf or TEAMID_TICKER_SHORT.pdf.

Anonymous review: use your registered Team ID only. No school names, team mem=
ber names, logos, or identifying metadata anywhere in either file.

Include on your cover page

Long or short; company name, ticker, and exchange.

Current price and reference date; market capitalization and enterprise value.

Price target and IRR over your stated holding period.

A three-line thesis summary.

Idea quality
Investability, risk and reward, business and management quality, and variant =
view.
Research
Quality of research and materials used, plus your view on additional diligenc=
e.
Written material
Clear, concise writing that strongly supports the investment thesis.

Team eligibility

Registered investment/finance clubs at the eight Ivy League institutions may =
enter two teams per school in Round 1; one team per school advances to the fi=
nal rounds.

Each team must have 4 currently enrolled undergraduates, with at most 2 senio=
rs, at least 1 sophomore, and at least 1 male and 1 female. All members must =
be listed at registration. Substitutions after the Round 1 deadline require c=
ommittee approval.

Faculty and alumni may advise on process and provide feedback, but may not wr=
ite, edit, or build any part of the submission. Disclose each advisor=E2=80=
=99s name and role.

Read the full rules & judging criteria

Before submitting: check your filenames, remove all identifying information, =
and include both your memo and financial model.

Submit your Round 1 pitch
Deadline: Sunday, October 25, 2026 =C2=B7 11:59 PM ET

Questions? Reply to this email.

Best,
The IIC Team

